---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Poured"
	description="What Poured is and how to use it."
	pubDate={new Date('September 14 2026')}
>
	<p>
		Poured is a practical journal for resin art beginners. Every guide answers one
		question completely: what to buy, how to pour it, or how to fix it when it
		goes wrong.
	</p>

	<h2>What you'll find here</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Getting started</strong> — kits, supplies, and your first pours.</li>
		<li><strong>Techniques</strong> — ocean waves, jewelry, molds, colorants.</li>
		<li><strong>Troubleshooting</strong> — bubbles, sticky cures, and every other failure mode, diagnosed.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>What you won't find</h2>
	<p>
		Sponsored product picks, 3,000-word intros before the answer, or gallery
		pieces with no instructions. If a guide doesn't save you a ruined pour,
		it doesn't belong here.
	</p>

	<h2>How to use the site</h2>
	<p>
		New to resin? Start with the three guides in <strong>Start in this order</strong> on
		the homepage. Stuck on something specific? Head to the guides archive and
		search for the symptom. New guides land weekly.
	</p>
</Layout>
